In a company, there are two types of employees: commissioned employees and hourly employees.

Employee that includes three instance variables—a first name (type String), a last name (type String) 

and a monthly salary (double). Commissioned employees earn a certain percentage of their total 

sales. Hourly employees receive wages based on the number of hours they have worked. Write an 

abstract class called Employee that contains the basic information about employees. The class 

should contain at least one abstract method called salary(). Write two concrete subclasses of 

Employee named CommissionedEmployee and HourlyEmployee. Write proper bodies in these 

classes to override the abstract method of their super class. Also include proper variables, getters, 

setters, constructors and exception handling mechanisms in all the classes.
